0..69 Comment "//! No rule of a family moves a term from one width to another width."
70..73 Comment "//!"
74..151 Comment "//! A rule relates two terms of one type. A family is one type at each index."
152..228 Comment "//! A rule that gives a bit for a word relates two terms of two types, and a"
229..255 Comment "//! term then has no type."
256..259 Comment "//!"
260..337 Comment "//! The checker reads the index of each node of each rule, and it refuses the"
338..417 Comment "//! family by the first rule that breaks an index. It refuses a case that gives"
418..496 Comment "//! two answers on the two sides of a rule of a family, as for any other type."
497..500 Comment "//!"
501..517 Comment "//! - see: #8338"
